id: pm-ajaskl
title: "GH-779: invalidate history drift cache after item and repair mutations"
description: "History validation can keep serving cached chain mismatches after the underlying item and history streams are clean, blocking strict governance gates until unrelated runtime GC."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T22:01:00.515Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T00:12:06.836Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T00:12:03.975Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Every committed item or history mutation invalidates the affected drift-cache entry; Successful and skipped-clean history repair cannot leave stale mismatches; Validate and health re-read current clean streams without global cache GC
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make cached governance evidence coherent with the mutation transaction
value: Strict integrity gates reflect current tracker truth instead of stale derived state
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Implemented shared best-effort drift-cache invalidators and authoritative bulk-repair source scans across append, rewrite, rollback, and repair paths."
expected_result: "History drift validation must immediately reflect every append, rewrite, rollback, and bulk repair without stale drift-cache or metadata-index false positives."
actual_result: All history mutation paths invalidate drift caches; authoritative bulk repair forces source scanning and invalidates skipped-clean candidates; live validation reports zero drift.
