comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T22:01:00.515Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: all-status searches for GH-779 and history drift cache invalidation found no canonical item; closed pm-7n8v owns GC scope only and closed pm-4a7m owns SDK history primitives."
  "2026-07-27T22:03:00.522Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/779. Claimed for the broad SDK governance and history-integrity bundle."
  "2026-07-27T23:31:45.466Z","harness:codex","Final verification evidence: lint, zero-warning static quality, TypeScript checking, contracts, docs/skills, context evaluation, secret scanning, and dependency audit passed. Full sandboxed coverage passed 380 files and 6,436 tests at exactly 100% statements (44,686/44,686), branches (31,786/31,786), functions (9,153/9,153), and lines (43,399/43,399). A packed tarball installed in a fresh unrelated consumer resolved its own CLI for npm/npx/bunx, completed init/create/claim/update/lean-output/health/validate/merge-install flows, and exercised the real Git merge driver across independent branches. Live repository health has zero warnings and authoritative history validation reports 0 missing, unreadable, hash-mismatch, or chain-mismatch streams."
  "2026-07-28T00:03:24.782Z","harness:codex","Review round 1: CodeRabbit identified that event-index maintenance could run before drift-cache invalidation and that non-missing cache removal failures were silent. Invalidation now runs immediately after every committed append; non-ENOENT failures emit a stable warning without rolling back history. A forced post-append event-index failure proves the committed stream remains and the cache is gone."
  "2026-07-28T00:12:00.660Z","harness:codex","Review round 1 terminal verification: focused SDK/CLI/history regressions, typecheck, lint, zero-duplicate/static quality, and full sandboxed coverage pass. Exact final suite is 380 files and 6,437 tests at 100% statements (44,702/44,702), branches (31,811/31,811), functions (9,149/9,149), and lines (43,418/43,418)."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T23:31:51.164Z","harness:codex",Integrity workflows must invalidate both derived history drift results and item-metadata indexes; invalidating only one cache can turn clean source documents into persistent false-positive repair candidates.
